                    <h3>BBA Project Report Format Explained</h3>
                    <p>A standard <span class="keyword">BBA project report format</span> typically includes:</p>
                    
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Title Page:</strong> Project title, student details, guide name</li>
                        <li><strong>Certificate:</strong> Completion certificate from college</li>
                        <li><strong>Acknowledgement:</strong> Thanks to guides and supporters</li>
                        <li><strong>Table of Contents:</strong> Organized chapter listing</li>
                        <li><strong>Chapter 1 – Introduction:</strong> Basic problem statement and objectives</li>
                        <li><strong>Chapter 2 – Literature Review:</strong> Simple review of existing studies</li>
                        <li><strong>Chapter 3 – Methodology:</strong> Basic research design</li>
                        <li><strong>Chapter 4 – Analysis:</strong> Simple data interpretation</li>
                        <li><strong>Chapter 5 – Findings & Conclusions:</strong> Basic findings and suggestions</li>
                        <li><strong>Bibliography:</strong> Reference list</li>
                        <li><strong>Appendices:</strong> Questionnaire, raw data</li>
                    </ul>
                    
                    <div class="center-highlight">
                        <p><strong>Note:</strong> BBA projects typically range from 60‑80 pages, significantly shorter than MBA projects which can be 80‑120 pages.</p>
